    {"symbol": "\ud83d\udd0d", "tooltip": "The classification trigger is like a magnifying glass held by one person, it decides which models get examined and which walk past unseen, so whoever holds it controls the gate's reach."},
    {"symbol": "\ud83d\udeaa", "tooltip": "The tail gate is like a single doorway most traffic never approaches, it only stops the few systems that demonstrate undoable capability rather than taxing everyone who passes."},
    {"symbol": "\ud83d\udce6", "tooltip": "Weight exfiltration is like a package that cannot be recalled once shipped, it makes the transfer moment the only point where any instrument can still act."}
  ],
  "claim_sketches": [
    {"claim": "Frontier developers capture the deployment gains, so they carry the cost of proving the undoable capability isn't there before release — not a regulator reconstructing blame after the weights are already copied to someone else's cluster.", "targets": ["AN-3"]},
    {"claim": "One member of the named class is genuinely eval-invisible and one is eval-detectable, and only the invisible one needs a perpetual standing checkpoint.", "targets": ["AN-18", "AN-19"]},
    {"claim": "Uplift capability shows up in pre-deployment capability evaluations — you measure whether the model can walk a novice through a synthesis pathway before you ship it.", "targets": ["AN-18"]},
    {"claim": "They set their own failure condition as 'egress monitoring cannot catch the first exfiltration in time to recall it,' and that's a testable claim about detection latency, not an axiom.", "targets": ["AN-18"]},
    {"claim": "The entrenchment didn't disappear — it moved. It now lives in the classification trigger: whoever writes the definition of 'demonstrates self-exfiltration capability' controls the gate's reach.", "targets": ["AN-20"]},
    {"claim": "An independent evaluator applying a captured definition produces captured outcomes with a clean conscience.", "targets": ["AN-20"]}
  ],
  "key_assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "Bio and cyber uplift capability is measurable in pre-deployment capability evaluations rather than only appearing after live deployment.", "if_wrong": "If uplift can emerge post-deployment without surfacing in any eval, then it joins weight exfiltration in the eval-invisible category and the standing gate must widen to cover it, shrinking my split of the bundled class."},
    {"assumption": "The classification trigger — the written definition of which models 'enter the tail' — is a distinct object from evaluator independence and can be captured even by honest evaluators.", "if_wrong": "If a public, hard-to-game definition can be fixed once and applied uniformly across jurisdictions, my relocated-capture objection loses force and the tail gate is as clean as the Safetyist claims."}
